{:id :EACL-FORMAL-064
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :benchmark
 :seed-or-trace
 "datascript/lookup-page/cache-bypass/relationship-width"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :performance
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 commit e50f1cb5395e105edf3875d50e0afb16b1ba7cee"]
 :affected-backends [:datascript]
 :root-cause
 "Cursor construction supplied the permission relation closure to a content digest, so even a cache-bypassed seven-item demand page scanned the entire authorization graph merely to mint its cursor."
 :fix
 "Use the supported-writer ordered-generation proof frame. Cursor minting reads only the complete dependency generations and stores the scalar frontier, so unrelated later transactions remain valid without relationship-content scans while relevant writes reject the cursor."
 :closing-evidence
 ["ScalarFrontierCoherence.UnrelatedMutationPreservesFrontier"
  "ScalarFrontierCoherence.RelevantMutationAdvancesFrontier"
  "eacl.datascript.enumeration-routing-test/ordered-generation-cursors-avoid-relationship-content-scans-test"
  "eacl.datascript.enumeration-routing-test/acyclic-relevant-write-rejects-current-only-cursor-test"
  "eacl.bench.explorer-enumeration-test/explorer-10000-user-page-does-not-scale-with-denotation"]}
